* The submarine rescues swimmers (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own
* script). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to
* repeat.
*
* Owner, 2026-11-17 (picture submarine-rescue-path.webp): while the
* submarine is moving along its path, it should scoop up any creature that
* is under water anywhere near it and deliver it safely out of the water.
*
* The submarine (vehicle 3 1 2) runs between its docks: from the east dock
* (x 7150-7160, top 810-820) down to a top of 935, west along the sea
* above the seabed to x 6065, and up to the west dock (top 790); from
* there down the shaft and east through the tunnel under the seabed (top
* 1255) to its dock below (x 6465, the airlock, drained as it docks); and
* back. It moves 5-10 px a tick and its box is 222 x 166. It lets its
* passengers out at each dock, onto dry floor (NOTES: "Submarine").
*
* A watcher (2 1 162, every 2 ticks) looks at the submarine. While it is
* moving (any speed), every live creature wholly under the waterline (top
* below y 710: not one in a boat or on a dock, though the sea's rooms
* start about 30 px above the waterline drawn) in a water room with its
* middle within 200 px of the submarine's box is drawn toward the
* submarine's middle, 16-24 px a step in each direction (moved by script,
* so no fall to learn from), and once its middle is inside the box the
* submarine takes it aboard (GPAS: the engine puts it in the cabin). It
* rides to the next dock and is let out there with everyone else.
enum 2 1 162 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 162 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1350 tick 2 slow
scrp 2 1 162 9
  inst
* var0 the submarine (var5 1 once found moving), var1-var4 its box
  setv var5 0
  enum 3 1 2
    doif velx ne 0 or vely ne 0
      setv var0 targ
      setv var1 posl setv var2 post setv var3 posr setv var4 posb
      setv var5 1
    endi
  next
  doif var5 eq 0 stop endi
* var5 2 when someone is ready to board; var6, var7 a creature's middle
  enum 4 0 0
    doif dead eq 0 and rtyp eq 2 and post ge 710
      setv var6 posl addv var6 posr divv var6 2
      setv var7 post addv var7 posb divv var7 2
      setv var8 var1 subv var8 200
      setv var9 var3 addv var9 200
      doif var6 ge var8 and var6 le var9
        setv var8 var2 subv var8 200
        setv var9 var4 addv var9 200
        doif var7 ge var8 and var7 le var9
          doif var6 ge var1 and var6 le var3 and var7 ge var2 and var7 le var4
            setv var5 2
          else
*           (never through the seabed: east of the shaft, x 6391, the sand
*           at y 1175 parts the open sea from the tunnel under it, which
*           the submarine also runs along to its dock below)
            setv var8 0
            doif var6 gt 6391
              setv var9 var2 addv var9 var4 divv var9 2
              doif var9 lt 1175 and var7 gt 1175 setv var8 1 endi
              doif var9 gt 1175 and var7 lt 1175 setv var8 1 endi
            endi
            doif var8 eq 0
            rndv var9 16 24
*           across, toward the submarine's middle
            setv var8 var1 addv var8 var3 divv var8 2 subv var8 var6
            doif var8 gt var9 setv var8 var9 endi
            negv var9
            doif var8 lt var9 setv var8 var9 endi
            negv var9
            mvby var8 0
*           and up or down
            setv var8 var2 addv var8 var4 divv var8 2 subv var8 var7
            doif var8 gt var9 setv var8 var9 endi
            negv var9
            doif var8 lt var9 setv var8 var9 endi
            mvby 0 var8
            setv velx 0 setv vely 0
            endi
          endi
        endi
      endi
    endi
  next
  doif var5 eq 2
    targ var0
    gpas
  endi
endm
